WEBVTT

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:22.660
Alpha to eagle one. Come in one. Alpha to eagle one. Come in one.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.830
Paul, we're returning to Alpha.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:34.000
Turning?

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.070
We had a close call.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.990
We were descending to the planet surface at normal speed,

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.170
and suddenly we were pulled down at tremendous speed,

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.990
as if the G-forces had increased enormously.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.180
I've checked that out, John.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.180
G-forces remained constant.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.620
No other force was recorded on the instruments, Commander.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.320
Whatever force it was, it wasn't anything we know about.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.990
Did you get that, Paul?

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.980
the power we had to get away.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.740
them, crash down in a crater.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.180
Over a hundred miles from here.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.020
Three are alive, Paul.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.140
I can't get a reading from Commander Koenig.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:42.790
Bob, this medical monitor is not registered.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:43.930
Russell.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:46.600
We're on our way.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.680
Paul, any word from them yet?

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:58.820
Nothing, Doctor.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:08.940
Still no life ratings. Keep me posted, Paul.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:39.580
VEHICLE FORWARD!

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:29.700
Commander Koenig, that's Carter, Paul.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:35.140
Yeah, but the commander's hurt pretty bad.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:08.340
Do what you can, Alan. A rescue unit's on its way. We'll have you home in no time.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:11.850
Dr. Russell.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:16.880
Thank you, Paul.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:42.300
Hall, it's Commander Koenig.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.780
Alongside now.

00:09:31.372 --> 00:09:32.272
Don't move anyone.

00:09:32.748 --> 00:09:33.608
until I've examined them.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.280
We can't do anything more for them here.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:02.360
We've got to get them back to Alpha.

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:02.740
Paul.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:06.950
Yes, Alan.

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:07.430
Go ahead.

00:11:12.390 --> 00:11:14.830
Separate this section from the rest of the Eagle and have it carried back.

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.080
Affirmative.

00:12:03.388 --> 00:12:03.888
Oh!

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.770
Hope you enjoy your stay here on Zenho, Commander Kearney.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:20.430
must be exhausted after your long walk. It's not a dream, but all very real, I assure you. This is

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:27.240
the planet Zeno, a major planet in the solar system known as Crichton, five million light

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:29.980
years away from Earth. We had our computer check out every...

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:31.880
They're all dead.

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:33.550
Yes, of course.

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:38.920
Your primitive machinery would record that fallacy simply because I ordered it to.

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:40.140
Expect me to believe that.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:41.790
Why should I lie?

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:47.790
You are also thinking that our scanner system located your moon, and you were brought here

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:48.470
by spaceship.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:49.860
That is correct.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:51.950
You can read your mind.

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:53.400
All Xenites care.

00:15:54.110 --> 00:15:55.910
We have no use of mechanical devices.

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:59.670
What we need or want, we create with our mind.

00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:02.770
The mind is master of all things.

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:05.640
This is my home.

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:07.340
It is made of light.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:09.840
Outside is our city.

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:11.530
One of many.

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:17.190
Still skeptical.

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:21.150
Another view?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:23.690
Close one there.

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:29.960
You will adjust to it in time.

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.430
A city of light.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.350
Light is alive.

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:38.470
Color is alive.

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:49.070
Allow me to impress you even further.

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:56.210
My name is Ran, as human as you are.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:05.750
This must be a dream.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:09.870
No, Commander. It all happened here on Zeno.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:11.480
I made it happen.

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:13.090
See for yourself.

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:35.340
Why am I here? The inevitable question.

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:36.970
Because.

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:41.650
Because, Commander, my father is the foremost anthropologist on Zeno.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.470
You have not met formerly.

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:15.360
Werner, may I present Commander Koenig?

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:17.900
Commander Koenig, my daughter Werner.

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:28.870
Like all scientists, my father's curiosity is insatiable.

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:31.840
He wants to learn from you.

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:41.900
Not about the present or the future, but the past.

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:47.430
And now let us make you feel more comfortable, more at home.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:06.100
I'm sorry it's not the real thing, only an image of it, but quite accommodating nevertheless.

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:10.260
I take it I'm a prisoner here.

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:16.060
No, no, no. You are a guest in my home.

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:17.420
Permanent.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.890
Unfortunately, your life span is only one-tenth of ours.

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:40.100
You don't see what you hope to learn from me.

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:43.700
I want to know your mind, the mind of an earth.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:49.030
All our ancient books, though very informative, are limited in knowledge.

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:55.630
But you, dear Commander Koenig, flesh and blood, you're real.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:59.030
I've been searching for such as you for a long time.

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:09.560
You are our missing link.

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:22.420
Sir, have the motor away.

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:25.960
And they've secured the module. I'll take over from here.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.980
You just keep your fingers crossed.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:40.730
Your food, Commander.

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.730
You must eat.

00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:53.680
I suggest you resign yourself to the situation.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:59.980
My being...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.980
Consider the caveman of the future as your idea of a situation?

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:04.800
Do you know what your father intends to do?

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:07.780
To use me as an experiment as if I were some kind of...

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:09.870
Some kind of animal.

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:10.600
Exactly.

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:15.780
Yes, I've read of Earth people and their experiments with animals,

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:20.460
exposing their brains and implanting electrical devices

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:22.730
to record their thought process.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:25.630
But if that is all he wanted to learn from you,

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:28.370
he would simply read your mind, as I would.

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:29.980
The principle is...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.960
Exactly the same. I am being kept here against my will for scientific research.

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:37.630
What your father proposes is just as inhumane.

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:41.500
Have the Zenites progressed beyond principle?

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:46.020
I assure you, no harm will come to you.

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:52.430
Vanna, I'm not a Zenite. What's not harmful to you may be to me.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:57.640
And you can tell your father I'll do everything I can to get back to Alpha.

00:21:58.240 --> 00:21:58.940
That is impossible.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:02.340
You will remain here till the end of your life.

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:05.230
And that day will come a lot sooner.

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:17.160
Ready for pickup.

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:20.600
Countdown, 10 seconds.

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:28.840
9, 8, 7, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:23.530
My first experiment, turning you to Alpha.

00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:34.350
It's all right. You're safe now.

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:47.750
You've been unconscious for two days.

00:24:01.660 --> 00:24:07.420
Codwin made it through all right, but Sandra's dead.

00:24:11.290 --> 00:24:15.250
Lena did everything she could to save her, but it meant nothing.

00:24:16.340 --> 00:24:17.820
You know, the whole thing's ridiculous.

00:24:18.080 --> 00:24:21.240
I mean, we're always going to die.

00:24:22.620 --> 00:24:24.320
Slowly, one by one.

00:24:26.380 --> 00:24:27.100
No use.

00:24:30.860 --> 00:24:34.770
Victor, the same way about Sandra.

00:24:37.720 --> 00:24:41.100
You'll know that death's a way of life with us now.

00:24:42.760 --> 00:24:44.040
Don't philosophize, John.

00:24:44.340 --> 00:24:45.040
Not with me.

00:24:45.220 --> 00:24:46.360
I'm not talking about Sandra.

00:24:47.220 --> 00:24:47.960
I'm talking about everything.

00:24:49.950 --> 00:24:51.790
When are we going to stop killing ourselves?

00:24:55.100 --> 00:24:56.060
Get off this rock.

00:24:57.020 --> 00:24:58.540
This is our tomb.

00:24:59.410 --> 00:24:59.970
We walk about...

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:14.120
here breathing but we're not living we're existing i want to live like a human being again oh no

00:25:14.120 --> 00:25:25.570
not you you're a big man around here as if you play god every day huh where are you going

00:25:34.880 --> 00:25:42.580
If you want to check yourself out, that's your affair.

00:25:43.280 --> 00:25:44.120
Open any airlock.

00:25:44.820 --> 00:25:45.120
No!

00:26:00.700 --> 00:26:02.140
We can start living again.

00:26:05.960 --> 00:26:11.340
Waiting for us, John.

00:26:17.470 --> 00:26:18.250
It's another way to die.

00:26:18.850 --> 00:26:19.210
Paul!

00:27:31.950 --> 00:27:34.750
Victor, help me, Victor. Help me.

00:27:36.430 --> 00:27:37.920
Hey, hey, Victor!

00:28:01.660 --> 00:28:09.100
The sphere of my experiment manifested itself in strange, repulsive creatures who appeared real and alive to him.

00:28:10.660 --> 00:28:13.360
But it is violence I find most fascinating.

00:28:14.270 --> 00:28:16.530
I find violence very disturbing.

00:28:17.590 --> 00:28:18.370
It is frightening.

00:28:19.640 --> 00:28:25.320
Had I been present when he realized Professor Bergman was merely an image, I do believe he would have taken my life.

00:28:27.420 --> 00:28:29.960
I can see how the ancient books do not exaggerate.

00:28:31.400 --> 00:28:39.050
Murder, war, violence beyond description is a way of life for Earth man.

00:28:39.770 --> 00:28:41.410
Perhaps he will prove too dangerous.

00:28:42.050 --> 00:28:43.950
He may truly kill one of us.

00:28:44.710 --> 00:28:46.570
You should neutralize his mind.

00:28:47.520 --> 00:28:49.100
You may go too far.

00:28:50.120 --> 00:28:55.160
No, I can create situations for him, but his reactions must be true.

00:28:56.080 --> 00:28:57.720
And his choice of dealing with them free.

00:28:57.900 --> 00:28:59.800
Otherwise, there'd be no point in making the experiment.

00:29:01.180 --> 00:29:05.430
He must neutralize his own mind, conquer his violence.

00:29:39.280 --> 00:29:40.620
There were four of us in that crash.

00:29:42.070 --> 00:29:52.900
Three will survive, and why can't it be me or Sandra?

00:29:56.150 --> 00:29:59.550
It may simply be John's time to die.

00:30:13.400 --> 00:30:23.060
Commander, it was very wise to realize that your friend was not real.

00:30:24.400 --> 00:30:25.580
But I do not see how you knew.

00:30:27.840 --> 00:30:29.180
Victor would never give up on himself.

00:30:30.510 --> 00:30:31.670
I wanted him to be real.

00:30:32.600 --> 00:30:35.420
Otherwise, I would have seen through your father's deception much sooner.

00:30:36.380 --> 00:30:37.920
We are incapable of deception.

00:30:40.420 --> 00:30:45.030
Every scientist makes that claim and justifies the means.

00:30:45.820 --> 00:30:47.760
I'm too young to understand my father's reasoning,

00:30:47.820 --> 00:30:51.090
but I know his intention was not to deceive you.

00:30:52.090 --> 00:30:54.710
We Zenites are born free of negative emotions,

00:30:55.370 --> 00:30:58.750
thereby bringing us tranquility and peace.

00:30:59.540 --> 00:30:59.980
You see...

00:31:00.060 --> 00:31:03.440
However, it does not come easily or swiftly.

00:31:04.460 --> 00:31:04.680
You're lucky.

00:31:17.670 --> 00:31:21.520
We feel such joy because we understand hate.

00:31:23.290 --> 00:31:25.030
It is born of fear and we fear nothing.

00:31:25.680 --> 00:31:26.260
Except death.

00:31:26.810 --> 00:31:27.970
We do not believe in death.

00:31:28.710 --> 00:31:29.970
Only in the continuing...

00:31:30.060 --> 00:31:37.750
flow of life therefore you're refusing food your choice to starve yourself is incomprehensible to

00:31:37.750 --> 00:31:49.450
me take you away from here against your will understand if you were to remain here of your

00:31:49.450 --> 00:31:59.300
own free will you also would understand clumsy fool

00:32:00.510 --> 00:32:02.130
Is it so difficult to carry a tray of coffee?

00:32:02.270 --> 00:32:03.110
That's enough, Karno.

00:32:07.730 --> 00:32:08.090
Inefficient.

00:32:08.290 --> 00:32:09.370
I said that's enough.

00:32:10.900 --> 00:32:11.380
You're right, Jim.

00:32:13.380 --> 00:32:14.160
Never do that again.

00:32:17.120 --> 00:32:17.380
You're not.

00:32:18.630 --> 00:32:19.740
Right duty.

00:32:20.650 --> 00:32:21.170
So are you.

00:32:23.930 --> 00:32:24.210
Paul.

00:32:29.280 --> 00:32:29.980
Everyone back to this.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:30.300
stations.

00:33:06.040 --> 00:33:06.820
Raise it three points.

00:33:07.710 --> 00:33:08.470
That could kill him.

00:33:10.220 --> 00:33:10.800
Three points.

00:34:18.400 --> 00:34:22.000
As a scientist, I owe it to humanity to learn all I can.

00:34:22.480 --> 00:34:26.640
It is the only way to help man, to bring him closer to his true destiny.

00:34:27.530 --> 00:34:29.390
But you can learn nothing from the commander.

00:34:30.220 --> 00:34:38.190
Because whatever image you present to him is unreal, so that his reaction, though honest, is unreal as well.

00:34:40.590 --> 00:34:47.840
To explore our own minds and the mind of the universe, for knowledge and understanding, that is a good thing.

00:34:48.680 --> 00:34:52.160
John Koenig is neither of these. He's an individual.

00:34:53.350 --> 00:34:54.830
His blood is our blood.

00:34:56.180 --> 00:34:57.780
We have no right to exploit him.

00:35:00.060 --> 00:35:05.690
me to send him back. I don't know.

00:35:09.550 --> 00:35:29.170
It's all so confusing. I was just thinking of you.

00:35:40.110 --> 00:35:40.490
I know.

00:35:46.120 --> 00:35:47.560
Able to project music with your mind?

00:35:49.690 --> 00:35:50.230
You like it.

00:35:56.240 --> 00:35:56.600
It's beautiful.

00:35:58.050 --> 00:35:58.470
So sad.

00:36:00.830 --> 00:36:02.110
I don't think sadness existed here.

00:36:04.740 --> 00:36:05.160
It does.

00:36:08.180 --> 00:36:15.310
I can't read your mind.

00:36:17.820 --> 00:36:22.340
I want you to stay with me.

00:36:36.880 --> 00:36:43.160
Dr. Russell, you must not let him die.

00:36:45.720 --> 00:36:47.360
The machine is keeping John alive.

00:36:47.910 --> 00:36:49.230
Not himself, not me.

00:36:50.050 --> 00:36:51.310
What difference does it make?

00:36:52.080 --> 00:36:53.160
He is still alive.

00:36:55.240 --> 00:36:56.380
John is already dead.

00:36:57.990 --> 00:36:59.010
His body is dead.

00:36:59.460 --> 00:36:59.960
And his...

00:37:02.810 --> 00:37:04.960
I can't deceive myself any longer.

00:37:08.400 --> 00:37:10.580
Please wait a while longer.

00:37:33.230 --> 00:37:36.960
Look, there are wonders out there beyond your imagination.

00:37:38.300 --> 00:37:40.060
Everything you've wished for on Earth.

00:37:40.220 --> 00:37:41.500
The good things I offer you.

00:37:42.650 --> 00:37:44.230
A world without fear.

00:37:45.310 --> 00:37:46.750
A world without fear.

00:37:50.300 --> 00:37:51.840
Not your world, Commander.

00:37:55.120 --> 00:37:56.140
It will be, Father.

00:37:56.710 --> 00:37:58.510
We are to be united as one.

00:38:02.970 --> 00:38:03.910
That is impossible.

00:38:06.350 --> 00:38:10.550
But you have taught me that love is the bridge between all worlds.

00:38:10.900 --> 00:38:14.680
Only when you know how to cross it, you have yet to learn the way.

00:38:19.350 --> 00:38:23.290
Do you presume that you can stand two million years of evolution?

00:38:27.140 --> 00:38:27.260
Aye.

00:38:33.550 --> 00:38:36.940
I've made my choice. I want to stay here with Vanna.

00:38:37.140 --> 00:38:48.980
The entire base is pulling for the commander to make it.

00:38:50.010 --> 00:38:51.390
See the effect it's having on people.

00:38:52.780 --> 00:38:55.200
Losing his temper. Me as well.

00:38:56.080 --> 00:38:58.040
The security men have broken up three brawls already.

00:38:58.220 --> 00:38:59.300
That is not the point.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:02.040
That is precisely the point, Alan.

00:39:02.960 --> 00:39:05.080
We need a leader, even if it's just a name.

00:39:05.680 --> 00:39:07.240
John lives? Well, that's fine.

00:39:07.800 --> 00:39:09.480
Even if it doesn't, people will adjust.

00:39:10.730 --> 00:39:12.650
It's the not knowing that's getting everybody down.

00:39:13.230 --> 00:39:16.520
Who's going to take over? You? Paul?

00:39:17.600 --> 00:39:23.200
Oh, no. Still breathing.

00:39:24.480 --> 00:39:26.540
While he is, for my money, he is still the commander.

00:39:57.320 --> 00:39:58.820
This is also a friend of yours.

00:40:11.490 --> 00:40:13.370
Commander does not believe you are real.

00:40:16.850 --> 00:40:18.810
I have instilled the facts into her mind.

00:40:19.440 --> 00:40:21.720
Where she is and the situation.

00:40:23.430 --> 00:40:24.190
Not her part in it.

00:40:25.160 --> 00:40:25.880
That I leave to you.

00:40:27.270 --> 00:40:28.190
It is true, Commander.

00:40:29.040 --> 00:40:29.860
I know you have decided.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.600
I decided not to return to Alpha.

00:40:33.420 --> 00:40:36.240
Father, did you have to bring Sandra here?

00:40:41.870 --> 00:40:46.670
See, my daughter believes your friend is real.

00:40:50.340 --> 00:40:55.150
She trusts you. I don't.

00:40:57.960 --> 00:40:59.040
Well, Commander Kearney.

00:41:00.440 --> 00:41:01.700
Let me offer some proof.

00:41:05.160 --> 00:41:15.640
There is my image of Sandra, my image of you.

00:41:18.220 --> 00:41:21.060
However, your image on Alpha is dying.

00:41:21.580 --> 00:41:23.140
Even I cannot sustain it in effort.

00:41:24.670 --> 00:41:26.130
Only one of you will survive.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:33.880
Dr. Russell is going to disconnect your life support system.

00:41:34.780 --> 00:41:35.900
He believes you are dead.

00:41:37.500 --> 00:41:41.880
No, you will not remember seeing the commander alive and well.

00:41:43.450 --> 00:41:45.450
The decision still belongs to Dr. Russell.

00:41:46.930 --> 00:41:49.210
I cannot influence that decision in any way.

00:41:50.510 --> 00:41:50.970
No one can.

00:41:54.640 --> 00:41:55.600
Brought Victor's image here.

00:41:57.720 --> 00:41:58.500
Why not Saunders?

00:41:59.530 --> 00:41:59.970
Saunders.

00:42:01.020 --> 00:42:05.420
